%S A399951 1,5,17,59,183,599,1854,5856,18184,56546,174577,538288,1653285,
%T A399951 5065716,15486891,47235194,143842606,437172342,1327092647,4021882828,
%U A399951 12177228191,36819286813,111239026257,335697056836,1012392843440,3050229782572,9184796426941,27634496396312,83103090805218
%N A399951 Sum of the sizes of the largest components over all functions on n unlabeled nodes.
%C A399951 Documentation including recurrences is at A217860, for trees, cycles of trees and maps. Quotient a(n)/A001372(n) gives average size of largest component, approximately 0.76n, where A001372(n) counts the number of nonisomorphic maps on n nodes, whose maximum component size is summed here to give a(n).
%D A399951 P. Flajolet and R. Sedgewick, Analytic Combinatorics, Cambridge University Press, 2009, page 480.
%H A399951 Marko Riedel, <a href="/A399951/b399951.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..512</a>
%H A399951 Marko Riedel, <a href="/A399951/a399951.maple.txt">Maple code for sequence</a>.
%H A399951 Marko Riedel, <a href="/A399951/a399951.png">Example image for n=4</a>.
%F A399951 a(n) = Sum_{j=1..n} (A399664(n, j) - A399664(n, j-1)) * j. - _Sean A. Irvine_, Sep 27 2026
%e A399951 For n=2: there are three maps, first, two loops, second, a two-cycle and third, an arrow pointing to a loop (fixed point). Sum the sizes of the largest component to get in order 1+2+2=5. Average is thus 5/3 = 5/6*2 giving 0.83n but this is the second value in the sequence.
%Y A399951 Cf. A001372, A217860, A399664.
%K A399951 nonn,new
%O A399951 1,2
%A A399951 _Marko Riedel_, Sep 16 2026
